e, it is important to note that a lack of essential nutrients can exacerbate the symptoms and progression of conditions such as ELA (Eosinophilic Esophagitis), highlighting the critical role that proper nutrition plays in overall health and disease management.", "CALCIUM AND VITAMIN D DEPLETION:Calcium and vitamin D depletion can occur after certain types of bariatric surgery, affecting bone health.", "GUIDELINES ON VITAMIN D REPLACEMENT:Guidelines on vitamin D replacement provide recommendations for managing vitamin D levels in patients undergoing bariatric surgery.", "M.ª CRISTINA CUERDA COMPÉS:Adjunct physician at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Marañón, specializing in nutritional support for eating disorders.", "MARTA MOTILLA DE LA CÁMARA:Adjunct physician at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Marañón, focusing on nutritional therapy.", "LOREDANA ARHIP:Dietitian-Nutritionist at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Marañón, providing dietary support for patients.", "TRASTORNO POR ATRACÓN:TRASTORNO POR ATRACÓN is an eating disorder that is characterized by recurrent episodes of binge eating, where individuals consume large quantities of food in a short period of time. Unlike other eating disorders, such as bulimia nervosa, individuals with trastorno por atracón do not engage in subsequent purging behaviors or inappropriate compensatory actions. This disorder often leads to significant distress for those affected. In summary, trastorno por atracón is defined by its compulsive eating episodes without the presence of purging, distinguishing it from other eating disorders.", "MUJERES ADOLESCENTES:Grupo demográfico que presenta una prevalencia significativa de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, especialmente en países occidentales.", "MODELOS:Grupo profesional que parece estar más afectado por trastornos de la conducta alimentaria debido a presiones sociales sobre la imagen corporal.", "ATLETAS:Grupo profesional que también muestra una mayor incidencia de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, posiblemente debido a la presión para mantener un peso específico.", "GIMNASTAS:Grupo profesional que se encuentra en riesgo elevado de desarrollar trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, similar a modelos y atletas.", "BAJA AUTOESTIMA:La baja autoestima es un factor de riesgo significativo para el desarrollo de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, afectando a muchos pacientes."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}